{"study_accession":"PRJNA658707","secondary_study_accession":"SRP278483","title":"CD4+ T cell fate in multiple myeloma","description":"The average age of onset of multiple myeloma (MM) is in the 7th decade coinciding with the development of immunosenescence. As a consequence, lymphocyte recovery after lymphopenia-inducing anti-MM therapies (most notably autologous stem cell transplant) is reliant on homeostatic proliferation of peripheral T cells rather than replenishment by new thymic emigrants. Knowing the phenotypic changes in the T cell population over the course of disease, RNAseq was utilised to analyse the genotypic changes in order to further explore the fate of CD4+ T cells in MM with disease progression.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":4,"study_labels":[{"level":"study","event_code":"HSCT","certainty":"history","delta_days":-60.0,"delta_bucket":"B_FAR","time_precision":"approx","stage":"teacher","confidence":1.0,"evidence":"As a consequence, lymphocyte recovery after lymphopenia-inducing anti-MM therapies (most notably autologous stem cell transplant) is reliant on homeostatic proliferation of peripheral T cells rather than replenishment by new thymic emigrants.","model_version":"teacher:mlx:mlx-community/Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct-4bit"}],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN15887269","study_accession":"PRJNA658707","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"Healthy donor VBDR 413","description":"Healthy donor VBDR 413","sex":"missing","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2020-08-27","attributes":[["isolate","VBDR 413"],["age","missing"],["biomaterial_provider","ACRF Translational Research Laboratory"],["sex","missing"],["tissue","PBMC"],["cell_type","CD4 T cell"],["disease","normal"],["treatment","nil"],["RNA concentration (pg/ul)","1633"],["RIN","9.8"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR12495868","experiment_accession":"SRX8987358","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina Hi